      "exercise": "137", "groupId": "g1", "group": "review",
      "parts": [
        {"label": "a", "unknowns": "u = first/north team speed, v = second/east team speed, both nonnegative", "equations": "16(u^2+v^2)=576; 4(u-v)=4.8; hence u^2+v^2=36 and u-v=1.2", "solve": "u=v+1.2; 2v^2+2.4v-34.56=0; v=3.6 or -4.8. Reject negative speed; u=4.8, v=3.6.", "expected": [4.8,3.6], "units": ["km/h","km/h"], "verification": "Distances 19.2 and 14.4 km; difference 4.8 km; 19.2^2+14.4^2=576=24^2."},
        {"label": "b", "unknowns": "u = first object speed, v = second object speed, both nonnegative", "equations": "225(u^2+v^2)=9; 6u=8v; u/v=4/3", "solve": "u=4t, v=3t; 25t^2=0.04; t=0.04. Reject negative root; u=0.16, v=0.12.", "expected": [0.16,0.12], "units": ["m/s","m/s"], "verification": "At 15 s distances 2.4 and 1.8 m give 2.4^2+1.8^2=9. Also 6*0.16=8*0.12=0.96 m."}
      ],
      "gradingAssessment": "Four independently labeled numerical speed targets can be graded numeric; units and first/second ordering must remain explicit."
